    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d112">

                <pb facs="0514" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg394"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">550 E 1/135: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Child</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-03-27T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 27,
                                1922—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 6:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>44. Department’s 33 of March 24. Impossible to inform Department currently and
                    accurately without going to Genoa, taking a code clerk and probably a secretary.
                    During the Conference all important responsible officials of the Italian Foreign
                    Office will be <pb facs="0515" n="395" xml:id="pg395"/> at Genoa. This will
                    permit me to continue to function as Ambassador to Italy and not oblige someone
                    to assume or be invested with the doubtful function as official conference
                    observer. If this meets your views please cable and explain how personal
                    accounts and necessary cable tolls are to be charged. I request Dominian, of
                    Rome consulate,<anchor n="12" xml:id="d112-f1"/> be instructed to report to me
                    temporarily, if I go to Genoa. Letter follows by courier.<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d112-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Child</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
